#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kword; Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:14
#, no-c-format
msgid "Overview"
msgstr "Resumit"

#. Tag: primary
#: basics.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "screen"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:17
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword;, like most &GUI; based programs, divides the window up into several "
"areas. Each area of the window is used to perform a group of similar "
"features. When you examine the &kword; window, it is divided into 5 major "
"areas:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:23
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"kde-frame\">The &kde; Titlebar</link> (which remains at the "
"top of all programs run under &kde;)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"mb\">The Menubar</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"tb\">An assortment of Toolbars</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"kde-docstruct\">The Document Structure Area</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:34
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<link linkend=\"da\">The Document Area</link>, including the rulers and "
"scrollbars."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:37
#, no-c-format
msgid "<link linkend=\"statb\">The Status bar</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:48
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kde; Titlebar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The &kde; titlebar sits on top of all applications run under &kde;. For more "
"information on the titlebar, please see the &kde; User Guide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Menubar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The menubar provides access to all of &kword;'s functions and options. Each "
"part of the &kword; menubar is detailed in the section entitled: <link "
"linkend=\"basic-menubar\">The Menubar</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Toolbars"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The toolbars provide shortcuts to commonly used functions. &kword; uses 8 "
"toolbars, with similar functions grouped together."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid "Document Structure Area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:71
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Document Structure</guilabel> area places individual types of "
"data into useful groups (pictures, tables, text, etc) to help you find the "
"correct data in a complicated document. For more information, see the "
"section on <link linkend=\"doc-structure\">Document Structure</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Statusbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:79
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The status bar provides important information during the editing of your "
"document. In the lower left corner, &kword; gives you the current page "
"number and the total number of pages. There will be helpful text shown in "
"the status bar whenever you hold the mouse over a menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:82
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The status bar can be toggled on and off. See the section on <link linkend="
"\"opt-ui\">Configure &kword; User Interface</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: basics.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Document Area"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "The document area consists of:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Horizontal and Vertical Rulers</emphasis> - The rulers can be used "
"to help you layout your document. For more information on rulers, see <link "
"linkend=\"rulers\">Using Rulers</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Scrollbars</emphasis> - The scrollbars are used to move through a "
"&kword; document quickly. The &kword; scrollbars functions similar to all "
"scrollbars in &kde; or &Windows;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:102
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The scrollbars can be toggled on and off. See the section on <link linkend="
"\"opt-ui\">Configure &kword; User Interface</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Tab Selector</emphasis> - This is used to select and place tab "
"stops in your document for easy formatting. For more information on tab "
"stops, see the section entitled <link linkend=\"tab-stops\">Using Tab Stops</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>Document View</emphasis> - This is the area of the screen which is "
"used to enter text. It shows you the current status of your document, and "
"allows you to adjust frames, select text, and cut and paste text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: basics.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using Rulers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: basics.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "rulers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Along the top and left edges of the document area, are a horizontal and a "
"vertical ruler."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "These rulers measure from the top left corner of the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each ruler has a bright area surrounded by a dark area. The bright area "
"shows the size and location of the currently edited frame on that page. As "
"you change frames, the bright area changes to reflect the new frame's "
"settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "The ruler can measure the page in many common units of measure including:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid "Millimeters (mm)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "Points (pt)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid "Inches (in)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid "Centimeters (cm)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "Decimeters (dm)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:152
#, no-c-format
msgid "Pica (pi)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "Didot (dd)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cicero (cc)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:157
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To change the units of the ruler, place the mouse cursor over one of the "
"rulers (either one), and click with the &RMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:161
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the units you want to use from the popup menu. You will notice both "
"rulers change to the new unit of measure."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may also notice two vertical arrows (one pointed up, the other pointed "
"down), on the left side of the bright area of the horizontal ruler. These "
"are used to adjust the margin of a paragraph. For more information, see the "
"section entitled <link linkend=\"format-para\">Formatting Paragraphs.</link>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Finally, you may see some black marks, which are not part of the ruler. They "
"may appear as L shaped, a Reverse-L, an Upside-down T, or an Upside-down T "
"with a dot in it. These are locations of tab stops. For more information see "
"the section entitled <link linkend=\"tab-stops\">Using Tab Stops</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To quickly format the page layout, you can right mouse click on either "
"ruler. A small sub menu will appear. Simply select <guilabel>Page Layout...</"
"guilabel>, and the <link linkend=\"page-format\">Page Layout Dialog box</"
"link> will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:184
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you don't want the rulers in your document area, they can be switched off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: basics.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Simply select <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Hide Rulers</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar. This will remove the rulers from "
"the document area. Simply select <menuchoice> <guimenu>View</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Rulers</guimenuitem></menuchoice> to display the "
"rulers again."
msgstr ""

